{"nodes": [{"id": "examples_voice_frontend_plain_readme_plain_html_frontend", "label": "Plain HTML frontend (voice sample)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "examples/voice/frontend-plain/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single-file layout is intentional: capture, WebSocket I/O and per-sender playback stay inspectable in one place without bouncing through framework abstractions, and the other five frontends factor that same logic into framework-shaped pieces for comparison."}, {"id": "examples_voice_frontend_plain_readme_voice_modes", "label": "Three voice modes: 1:1, group, room", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/voice/frontend-plain/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1:1 and group are press-and-hold PTT; room is an open-mic toggle where multiple speakers stream concurrently \u2014 which is the case that forces the per-sender playback design."}, {"id": "examples_voice_frontend_plain_readme_binary_frame_envelope", "label": "Binary frame envelope with senderUsername prefix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/voice/frontend-plain/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A length-prefixed sender name in front of the opus payload is what lets the playback module dispatch each chunk to the right per-sender MediaSource when several people talk at once."}, {"id": "examples_voice_frontend_plain_readme_http_ingress_singleton", "label": "HTTP-ingress singleton serving /static/plain/", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/voice/frontend-plain/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "examples_voice_frontend_plain_readme_plain_html_frontend", "target": "ex